---
import SocialLayout from '../../layouts/SocialLayout.astro';
---

<SocialLayout
  title="Space"
  description="The FRQNCY Space — principles, roadmap, research, and the open questions driving this network."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-8 space-y-12 pb-16">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-gold/70 font-body">The Space</p>
      <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl text-gold leading-tight">
        A network built on resonance, not extraction.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-text-dim leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        The Space is where FRQNCY Social comes out from behind the feed — the principles, the plan, the research, and the open questions. It's what we've committed to in writing, so you can hold us to it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-dim">
        Looking for the room where everyone talks?
        <a href="/social/g/townhall" class="text-gold hover:text-gold-light">That's the Townhall →</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Principles -->
    <section class="space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-gold border-b border-card-border pb-3">Principles</h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg text-gold">Portability first</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim leading-relaxed">
            Your posts, follows, and reputation belong to you. From day one you can export everything. By year two you can take it to another host.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg text-gold">No ads, ever</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim leading-relaxed">
            The business model is you paying us a little — not an advertiser paying us to extract from you. Written into the charter.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg text-gold">Calibrated conviction</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim leading-relaxed">
            Posts tagged to a project get a stance and a horizon. We resolve them. Reputation is earned by being right — scored with a Brier rule, not vibes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg text-gold">Transparent ranking</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim leading-relaxed">
            The feed formula is public. You can see the weights. Later you'll be able to tune them. Algorithmic choice, not algorithmic lock-in.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg text-gold">Moderation as care</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim leading-relaxed">
            Automated first pass (Llama Guard 3), trust-levels, community mods per channel, blameless post-mortems when things break.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg text-gold">Farcaster / Nostr / ATProto</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim leading-relaxed">
            The destination is a protocol-native network. The route is AT Protocol as primary bridge, Farcaster as a crypto side-channel, Nostr as a read path.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Tiles -->
    <section class="space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-gold border-b border-card-border pb-3">Explore the Space</h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a
          href="/social/space/roadmap"
          class="group rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-gold/5 to-accent/5 border border-gold/20 hover:border-gold/40 p-6 transition-colors"
        >
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/70">01 · Plan</p>
              <h3 class="font-heading text-2xl text-gold mt-2 group-hover:text-gold-light transition-colors">Roadmap</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-dim mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                The 24-month plan. Three phases. What ships when, and why.
              </p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-gold text-xl group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="/social/space/research"
          class="group rounded-2xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border hover:border-gold/40 p-6 transition-colors"
        >
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/70">02 · Research</p>
              <h3 class="font-heading text-2xl text-gold mt-2 group-hover:text-gold-light transition-colors">Research Paper</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-dim mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                Protocols, feed ranking, monetization — the full ~7,000-word paper behind every decision.
              </p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-gold text-xl group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="/social"
          class="group rounded-2xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border hover:border-gold/40 p-6 transition-colors"
        >
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/70">03 · Network</p>
              <h3 class="font-heading text-2xl text-gold mt-2 group-hover:text-gold-light transition-colors">Feed</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-dim mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                Where conversations live. Project-anchored, chronological, follow-graph primary.
              </p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-gold text-xl group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="/v2/explore.html"
          class="group rounded-2xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border hover:border-gold/40 p-6 transition-colors"
        >
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold/70">04 · Context</p>
              <h3 class="font-heading text-2xl text-gold mt-2 group-hover:text-gold-light transition-colors">Network Map</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-dim mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                The 133-topic, 604-resource corpus this network is anchored in. Browse the terrain.
              </p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-gold text-xl group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Open questions -->
    <section class="space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-gold border-b border-card-border pb-3">Open Questions</h2>
      <p class="text-text-dim leading-relaxed">
        A network gets built in conversation. Here are the questions we do not have clean answers to yet — and that the community can help shape.
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-4">
        <li class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5">
          <p class="font-heading text-gold">1 · How does personal conviction live without becoming competition?</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Tagging a post with a stance (bullish / neutral / bearish) is self-expression — it tells people where you stand. We removed the public leaderboard on cooperation-over-competition grounds. Open question: do people want a <em>private</em> journal of their own stances over time, or does any tracking drift back toward scoreboarding?
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5">
          <p class="font-heading text-gold">2 · Should private DMs go to the PDS or stay in Supabase forever?</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            ATProto has no mature DM Lexicon yet. Do we wait, ship a custom encrypted Lexicon, or accept that DMs are the one thing that never federates?
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5">
          <p class="font-heading text-gold">3 · What does a "channel" look like on ATProto?</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Farcaster has channels. Bluesky has custom feeds and (coming) communities. FRQNCY's project-anchored rooms need a home somewhere in that spectrum.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-xl bg-card-bg border border-card-border p-5">
          <p class="font-heading text-gold">4 · When (if ever) do we enable staked conviction markets?</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-dim mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            The research says: only after a crypto-attorney review and likely a regulated intermediary. But the demand signal from users will shape how fast we pursue that review.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="border-t border-card-border pt-8 text-sm text-text-dim">
      <p>
        The Space is updated when the network learns something. Have a principle to propose or a question to add?
        <a href="mailto:hello@frqncy.network?subject=Space%20contribution" class="text-gold hover:text-gold-light underline decoration-gold/40">
          Send it in
        </a>.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</SocialLayout>
